body:
I18nServicePlugin looks up the HTTP server using service name 'http-server', but the canonical registration is 'http.server' (and external RuntimeConfig.server only registers 'http.server'). This can prevent route self-registration in real runtimes where the alias isn't present. Prefer resolving 'http.server' first (and optionally falling back to 'http-server' for backwards compatibility).
```suggestion
          // Prefer canonical service name used by RuntimeConfig.server
          httpServer = ctx.getService<IHttpServer>('http.server');
        } catch {
          // Service not found under canonical name — expected in MSW/mock mode or legacy setups
        }

        if (!httpServer) {
          try {
            // Backwards compatibility: fall back to legacy alias
            httpServer = ctx.getService<IHttpServer>('http-server');
          } catch {
            // Service not found under legacy alias either
          }
        }
```
